  "title": "Reconquista and the fall of Granada",
  "summary": "Muslim forces conquered Visigothic Spain from 711. Over the following centuries Christian kingdoms pushed south until, by the mid-13th century, only Granada remained in Muslim hands. It fell to Isabella of Castile and Ferdinand of Aragon on 2 January 1492, ending what World History Encyclopedia calls a 770-year military effort. That spring in Granada the monarchs decreed the expulsion of Jews, and Moors were later forced to convert or leave.",
